 gaps:[["Large jet engines","The single hardest gap in the ledger. GTRE's Kaveri ran forty years and failed at 642% cost overrun; the Safran-GTRE AMCA partnership is India's attempt at the CFM route fifty years after Snecma took it. Azad Engineering and MTAR already make hot-section parts for GE and Safran — India supplies the components and not the engine","open"],["Commercial airliners","India has never built a commercial aircraft and has no programme. HAL builds military platforms; the civil certification path alone would take a decade","open"]],
