{n:"Submarine cable systems & repeaters",by:"SubCom, Alcatel Submarine Networks, NEC, HMN Tech",blocks:"Three or four firms build the physical internet backbone. India lands major cables and manufactures no cable, repeaters or wet plant.",in:"SubCom · Alcatel Submarine Networks · Prysmian · NTT",sec:"IT, Cloud & Telecom"},
{n:"Cable-laying & repair ships",by:"SubCom, Global Marine, Orange Marine, ASN, NTT WE Marine",blocks:"India owns no cable ship. Repairs to cables landing in India depend on foreign vessels under consortium agreements.",in:"SubCom · Alcatel Submarine Networks · Greek shipowners · Maersk",sec:"IT, Cloud & Telecom"},
{n:"Subsea production & pressure control",by:"SLB (OneSubsea, Cameron), TechnipFMC, Aker Solutions, Baker Hughes",blocks:"Deepwater trees, manifolds, umbilicals and BOPs. India operates deepwater fields and manufactures none of the hardware on the seabed.",in:"SLB · TechnipFMC · NOV · HD Hyundai",sec:"Subsea & Offshore Systems"},
{n:"Drilling equipment & blowout preventers",by:"NOV, SLB Cameron, Dril-Quip, MHWirth",blocks:"No rig gets built without this equipment. India drills at scale and manufactures none of it.",in:"NOV · SLB · ExxonMobil · Reliance",sec:"Oil & Gas Equipment"},
{n:"Tower crane systems & controls",by:"Liebherr, Manitowoc (Potain), Wolffkran, Comansa, Zoomlion",blocks:"The gating equipment on every high-rise site. ACE is India's only maker at that class and imports the control and anti-collision systems.",in:"Liebherr · Manitowoc · Holcim group · Caterpillar",sec:"Construction & Mining Equipment"},
{n:"Subsea installation & IRM vessels",by:"Subsea7, TechnipFMC, Saipem, Allseas, Oceaneering, McDermott",blocks:"Installing and maintaining anything on the seabed needs purpose-built vessels. India operates deepwater fields and owns none, so every intervention is contracted to a foreign fleet.",in:"Subsea7 · TechnipFMC · Aker Solutions · SubCom",sec:"Subsea & Offshore Systems"},
{n:"Premium tubular connections",by:"Vallourec (VAM) and Tenaris Blue",blocks:"The gas-tight thread that makes OCTG usable in deepwater and HPHT wells. India produces pipe at world scale and licenses the connection on the end of it.",in:"Tenaris · Vallourec · NOV · SLB",sec:"Oil & Gas Equipment"},
{n:"Deepwater work-class ROVs & subsea tooling",by:"Oceaneering, Subsea7, Saab Seaeye, Forum Energy",blocks:"Intervention ROVs with manipulators, purpose-built seabed tooling and umbilicals. India now builds inspection-class ROVs commercially through Planys and EyeROV; the deepwater intervention class above them remains foreign.",in:"Oceaneering · Subsea7 · TechnipFMC · Saipem",sec:"Subsea & Offshore Systems"},
{n:"Coater/developer systems",by:"Tokyo Electron",blocks:"Effectively a monopoly, paired with every lithography scanner, and inside Japan's export control regime.",in:"Tokyo Electron · ASML · Applied Materials · Canon",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Etch equipment",by:"Lam Research, Tokyo Electron, Applied Materials",blocks:"The step that physically shapes every transistor and enables 3D NAND and gate-all-around structures.",in:"Lam Research · Applied Materials · Tokyo Electron · SK hynix",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Fab process control & metrology",by:"KLA, Onto, Hitachi High-Tech",blocks:"Yield learning is what makes a fab economic rather than merely operational. India has no capability at fab class.",in:"KLA · ASML · Applied Materials · TSMC",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Switch & networking silicon",by:"Broadcom, Marvell, NVIDIA",blocks:"Most of the world's data centre fabrics run on Tomahawk and Jericho class silicon. India builds the systems and none of the chips.",in:"Broadcom · Marvell · NVIDIA · Ericsson & Nokia",sec:"IT, Cloud & Telecom"},
{n:"FPGAs & adaptive computing",by:"AMD (Xilinx) and Intel (Altera)",blocks:"A duopoly on export-controlled parts. DRDO, ISRO and every Indian defence electronics programme designs around imported FPGAs.",in:"AMD · Intel · BEL · Data Patterns",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Ultrasound transducer arrays",by:"Philips, GE HealthCare, Vermon, Blatek, Sonoscape",blocks:"The value-dense component in every ultrasound system. India runs the world's highest scan volumes and assembles systems around imported probes.",in:"Philips · Canon · Fujifilm · GE HealthCare",sec:"Healthcare & Life Sciences"},
{n:"Specialty foundry platforms (RF-SOI, FD-SOI)",by:"GlobalFoundries, TSMC, Samsung, Tower, UMC",blocks:"The platforms Indian fabless firms in RF, power and edge AI actually need. India's fab programme targets licensed mature logic and offers none of them.",in:"GlobalFoundries · STMicroelectronics · Qualcomm · UMC & PSMC",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Premium & luxury vehicle platforms",by:"Mercedes-Benz, BMW, Audi, Volvo, Lexus",blocks:"India's luxury market is barely 1% of 4.4 million annual car sales and has no domestic entrant. Tata owns Jaguar Land Rover, engineered in the UK.",in:"Mercedes-Benz Group · BMW Group · Volkswagen Group · Brembo",sec:"Automotive & Mobility"},
{n:"Automotive R&D centres without IP",by:"Mercedes MBRDI, BMW TechWorks, VW, Bosch, Continental in India",blocks:"India runs some of the largest automotive engineering centres in the world for foreign owners and holds none of the platform or software IP they produce.",in:"Mercedes-Benz Group · BMW Group · Volkswagen Group · Bosch",sec:"Automotive & Mobility"},
{n:"In-process gauging & machine metrology",by:"Marposs, Renishaw, Blum-Novotest, Jenoptik",blocks:"Measuring a part while the machine is still cutting it — the difference between making a precision part once and making it repeatably. Every precision gap in this ledger sits on top of it.",in:"Marposs · Hexagon AB · Carl Zeiss · Fortive",sec:"Machine Tools & Precision"},
{n:"Ceramic tile machinery",by:"Sacmi, System Ceramics, Siti B&T",blocks:"India is the world's second-largest tile producer and Morbi's presses, kilns and digital decoration are all Italian.",in:"Sacmi · FLSmidth · Holcim group · Bühler",sec:"Machine Tools & Precision"},
{n:"Precision robotics gearing",by:"Harmonic Drive, Nabtesco, Sumitomo",blocks:"Harmonic and cycloidal reducers gate every industrial robot arm. Indian integrators import all of them.",in:"Bonfiglioli · FANUC · ABB · Comau",sec:"Industrial Automation"},
{n:"Five-axis machining centres",by:"DMG Mori, Mazak, Makino, Okuma, Hermle, GROB",blocks:"Turbine blades, impellers, implants and airframe structures cannot be made without simultaneous five-axis machining, and the class is export-controlled for defence end-use. Ethereal Machines is the sole Indian builder.",in:"DMG Mori · Walter group · GE Aerospace · Silmax",sec:"Machine Tools & Precision"},
{n:"Machine tool spindles & linear motion",by:"IBAG, GMN, THK, HIWIN, NSK, Schaeffler",blocks:"Spindles, guideways and ballscrews go into every Indian-built machine tool and none are made in India — including inside Ethereal's five-axis machines.",in:"DMG Mori · FANUC · Georg Fischer · SKF group",sec:"Machine Tools & Precision"},
{n:"Custom AI accelerator design",by:"Broadcom (~70% of the market), Marvell, Alchip, GUC",blocks:"Turning a hyperscaler's architecture into working silicon. It is how Google's TPUs and OpenAI's accelerators get built, and the alternative to buying NVIDIA. India sells design services into it and owns none of the silicon.",in:"Broadcom · Marvell · NVIDIA · TSMC",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Consumer networking hardware",by:"TP-Link, D-Link, Netgear, Tenda",blocks:"Routers and access points terminating one of the world's largest broadband subscriber bases, held almost entirely by Chinese and Taiwanese brands. VVDN builds them as an ODM for others.",in:"D-Link · Broadcom · MediaTek · NTT",sec:"IT, Cloud & Telecom"},
{n:"Mission-critical public safety communications",by:"Motorola Solutions, Airbus, L3Harris, Hytera",blocks:"Radio and dispatch systems that police, fire and disaster response depend on when cellular fails. India builds military radios and imports the civil ones.",in:"Motorola Solutions · Ericsson & Nokia · Leonardo · Thales",sec:"Aerospace & Defence"},
{n:"CPU instruction set architecture",by:"Arm (mobile and increasingly data centre), Intel and AMD (x86)",blocks:"Every device assembled in India carries a royalty on an architecture India does not own. Localising the factory does not touch it. RISC-V is the only mechanism that does.",in:"Arm Holdings · Qualcomm · Apple · NVIDIA",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Semiconductor process technology licensing",by:"PSMC, UMC and a small set of second-tier foundries; TSMC, Samsung and Intel do not license",blocks:"A country without its own node must license one. India's first commercial fab at Dholera runs on Powerchip process technology, which is why it is Tier C — Indian plant, Indian capital, foreign process.",in:"PSMC (Powerchip) · UMC · GlobalFoundries · TSMC",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Automotive display panels & cockpit HMI",by:"AUO (BHTC), LG Display, BOE, Continental, Visteon",blocks:"Qualified, long-life displays in every vehicle built. India assembles millions of cars a year and imports every panel and cockpit module in them.",in:"AUO · Innolux · BOE & CSOT · Continental",sec:"Electronics & Displays"},
{n:"EUV mask blanks",by:"Hoya, with AGC and Shin-Etsu supplying a minority",blocks:"The glass substrate every photomask is written on, held close to a monopoly by one Japanese firm. It sits upstream of ASML and of every advanced fab on earth.",in:"Hoya Corporation · ASML · TSMC · Carl Zeiss",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Hard disk glass substrates",by:"Hoya",blocks:"Nearline and data centre storage depends on them and one supplier dominates. India assembles no drives and makes no substrates.",in:"Hoya Corporation · Western Digital · Seagate · Amazon",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Chlor-alkali ion exchange membranes",by:"Asahi Kasei (Aciplex), AGC (Flemion), Chemours (Nafion)",blocks:"A thin fluoropolymer film inside every membrane-cell chlorine plant. India runs one of the world's largest chlor-alkali industries entirely on imported membrane.",in:"Asahi Kasei · AGC · Daikin · Veolia",sec:"Chemicals & Materials"},
{n:"Fusion splicers",by:"Fujikura and Sumitomo Electric",blocks:"Nothing joins optical fibre without one. India lays fibre at national scale and imports every splicer and consumable used to do it.",in:"Fujikura · Sumitomo Group · Corning · SubCom",sec:"IT, Cloud & Telecom"},
{n:"High-temperature superconducting tape",by:"Fujikura, SuperPower, Shanghai Superconductor, THEVA, Faraday Factory",blocks:"REBCO tape is the enabling material for compact fusion magnets and next-generation MRI. India has magnet engineering and no tape production.",in:"Fujikura · Philips · Vacuumschmelze · GE Vernova Hitachi",sec:"IT, Cloud & Telecom"},
{n:"Aerospace-grade carbon fibre",by:"Toray, Hexcel, Mitsubishi Chemical, SGL, Solvay",blocks:"Export-controlled dual-use material. India was refused it and built its own precursor chemistry through NAL, DRDO and ISRO — capability that exists at programme scale and not at volume.",in:"Toray Industries · Boeing · Airbus · GE Aerospace",sec:"Chemicals & Materials"},
{n:"Precision data converters",by:"Analog Devices, Texas Instruments, Renesas",blocks:"ADC and DAC resolution gates radar, test instruments, medical imaging and industrial control. Three firms hold the high-precision tier, and India designs instruments around imported parts.",in:"Analog Devices · Texas Instruments · Fortive · Philips",sec:"Semiconductors & EDA"},
{n:"Industrial piezo printheads",by:"Epson, Kyocera, Fujifilm Dimatix, Ricoh, Konica Minolta, Xaar",blocks:"The head inside every industrial inkjet — textile printing, ceramic tile decoration, packaging. India leads globally in textile printing volume and is second in tiles, and imports every head.",in:"Seiko Epson · Sacmi · Fujifilm Holdings · Canon",sec:"Electronics & Displays"},
{n:"Quartz crystal timing devices",by:"Epson, Nihon Dempa Kogyo, Kyocera, Murata, TXC",blocks:"A crystal oscillator sits inside essentially every electronic product assembled in India. None are made here, and almost nobody names the dependency.",in:"Seiko Epson · Murata · Dixon · D-Link",sec:"Electronics & Displays"},
{n:"Engineering simulation & CAE software",by:"Ansys (Synopsys), Dassault SIMULIA, Siemens Simcenter, Altair (Siemens), COMSOL, MathWorks",blocks:"Every Indian certification programme — aircraft, launcher, vehicle, bridge, chip — generates its evidence in licensed foreign software. India has one of the world's largest engineering workforces and two simulation product companies.",in:"Dassault Systèmes · Synopsys · Siemens · Cadence Design Systems",sec:"Simulation & CAE"}
